// A string concatenation passed straight to a function, `g(a + b)`: the `+`
// builds a new block that nothing names, so it is a fresh argument like a
// fresh call. The binary node also covers int arithmetic, which makes no block,
// so the node only counts when is_concat says one operand is a string.

esc_tmp_bin(int a) {
  int ok = 0;
  if((import nkind)[a] == "bin") {
    ok = is_concat(a);
  }
} return int ok;
